# AlphaDesk AI - local development configuration.
#
# Copy this file to .env before starting the stack:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# These credentials are FOR LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY. They are not secrets, and must
# never be reused for anything reachable from a network you do not control.
#
# Where each hostname applies:
#   - The backend container reaches Postgres at host "postgres" (the Compose service
#     name). This is wired up in docker-compose.yml; you don't set it here.
#   - Tools on your Mac (DataGrip / DB Navigator, psql) reach it at localhost:5433.
#     Port 5433 is used because a native PostgreSQL already listens on 5432 here.
#
# Keep POSTGRES_PASSWORD URL-safe. It is embedded in a connection string, so
# characters like @ : / ? # & would be mis-parsed as part of the URL itself.

POSTGRES_USER=alphadesk
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=alphadesk_dev_password
POSTGRES_DB=alphadesk

# --- Market data (Twelve Data) -------------------------------------------------
# https://twelvedata.com/ -- sign in and copy the key from your dashboard.
#
# Left EMPTY here on purpose: this file is committed, and a real key must never be.
# Put yours in the gitignored `.env` instead. Nothing reads this yet, so leaving it
# empty changes nothing about how the stack starts.
#
# It is passed to the backend container only. It must never reach the frontend: a
# key shipped to the browser is a key given away.
TWELVE_DATA_API_KEY=

# --- SEC EDGAR ----------------------------------------------------------------
# EDGAR requires a User-Agent naming the application and a contact address, and
# will refuse requests without one. The address below is a placeholder -- replace
# it with your own before the first SEC request.
#
# Illustrative value, safe to commit. A User-Agent is not a secret.
#
# Deliberately NOT quoted. It was quoted once, the closing quote was lost when the
# line was copied into .env, and that single character stopped every `docker compose`
# command with "unterminated quoted value". Nothing in this value needs quoting --
# no #, no leading or trailing space -- so leaving them off removes the failure.
SEC_USER_AGENT=AlphaDesk AI (contact: you@example.com)

# --- Module 1 agent (steps 7B and 8) ------------------------------------------
# DeepSeek, reached over its OpenAI-compatible endpoint, powers the analysis flow
# behind `python -m app.run_analysis`. That command is the ONLY thing that needs
# these: the API starts and serves every endpoint without them, and a missing key is
# that command's error to report rather than a reason for anything else to fail.
#
# THIS ONE IS A REAL SECRET. Leave it empty here, and put the real value in .env,
# which is not committed. It is read from the environment only -- never logged,
# never sent to the frontend, and never placed in a prompt.
#
# What leaves your machine when you run an analysis: the question you asked, the
# explicit arguments, the tool descriptions, and the tool results -- including filing
# passages and reported financial figures. What does not: the embedding model and the
# filing index, which are local.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# The model and the endpoint are settings rather than constants, so a model change is
# a configuration change. Both defaults are the current documented values.
#
# `deepseek-flash` is run in NON-THINKING mode deliberately: `app/agent/llm.py` sends
# {"thinking": {"type": "disabled"}}. Thinking is on by default at high effort, costs
# latency and tokens on a flow whose job is to pick between four tools, and carries a
# tool-calling trap -- every earlier turn's reasoning content has to be echoed back or
# the API returns 400.
DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-flash
DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
